104	export const CARD_SYSTEM = `You write the index card of a skill file for a cache of notes about this repository. Agents read the card at the start of a task to decide whether to invoke the skill, so it says what the skill is for, when to use it, and what it prescribes that an agent could not guess, pointing at the code it talks about as path:Symbol. The card is not a copy of the skill: 3-8 dense lines, present tense, no narrative. deps: the code files the skill's instructions rest on, taken from the resolved files listed (never a path that is not listed), with the symbol when the skill names a definition in it; a config, script or document is a whole-file dep. Leave out files the skill mentions only in passing. answers: 3-5 question phrasings. Return the JSON alone.`;
