1	// The context proxy: an agent's requests to the Anthropic API pass through a local process that asks the API
2	// to clear old tool results on its side (`clear_tool_uses_20250919`, beta `context-management-2025-06-27`).
3	// Off unless someone starts it (`thinker proxy`) and points the agent at it (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL).
4	//
5	// Any client of the Messages API (2026-10-24): the edit needs the beta header, which Claude Code sends on every
6	// request and no other agent does (pi, OpenCode, Goose, Aider, Cline, Droid: checked on 2026-10-24, pi live). Until
7	// then a request without it was forwarded untouched (`no-beta`), so the proxy cleared for Claude Code alone; now the
8	// header is added upstream (`withBeta`, logged `betaAdded`) and the edit with it. The agent's own bytes are still
9	// not rewritten: a header is added, and a block appended to the body as before.
10	//
11	// Why the server's edit and not our own: on the models that run the preserved-thinking check (Opus 5.5,
12	// Sonnet 5.5, Haiku 5.5, Fable 5.1) a client-side rewrite of an earlier tool_result is an edited history,
13	// a 400 on enforced accounts and every later thinking block dropped elsewhere; the server's clearing is not
14	// counted as an edit. So the proxy keeps no state and rewrites nothing the agent sent: it appends one edit
15	// to `context_management.edits`, which Claude Code already sends (with `clear_thinking` alone).
16	//
17	// Seen live on 2026-10-20 (Claude Code 2.1.304, a subscription login): the cleared set is stable between
18	// clears, so the turns after a clear read the shorter prefix from the cache; a clear writes the cache again
19	// from the system prompt on, at 2x the input price (1-hour writes). The defaults are the replay's over
20	// 1,700 local sessions: 9.2% of billed-equivalent tokens saved, 29 sessions costlier, all of it in long
21	// sessions (14.7% over 120 requests, nothing under 60). The model's own reaction to the placeholders is not
22	// in that number; an experiment is.
23	import http from 'node:http';
24	import https from 'node:https';
25	import fs from 'node:fs';
26	import { ProxyAgent } from 'proxy-agent';
27	import path from 'node:path';
28	import crypto from 'node:crypto';
29	import { transformResponses, responsesUsageTap, responsesReport } from './proxy-responses.js';
30	import { CODEX_PROXY_PATH, CODEX_UPSTREAMS } from './proxy-codex.js';
31	import { foreignAuth } from './proxy-route.js';
32	import { noteCompression } from './compression.js';
