36	export const EDIT_TYPE = 'clear_tool_uses_20250919';
37	export const EDIT_BETA = 'context-management-2025-06-27';
38	// `keep`: how many of the newest tool uses a clear leaves, a count or `turn` (2026-10-22): the tool uses of the
39	// request's current turn, never under `keepMin`. The Context tab's measurement behind `turn`: on this repository's
40	// sessions 88% of what tool results cost is reading them again after the agent last used them, 82% after the turn
41	// that fetched them ended, and only 8% is a result used again later in its own turn (tool-outputs.js:sessionOutputs).
42	// A count clears results the agent is still working from in a long turn, and the model was seen to read the file
43	// again; `turn` clears only what earlier turns fetched, so it clears less and should cost the agent nothing. The
44	// server's edit takes a count alone, so the proxy works the count out from the request's messages on every call.
45	// `turn` is the default since 2026-10-22, the owner's decision on the replay alone (proxy-replay.js, 3,317 Claude Code
46	// sessions of this machine over 30 days): at this trigger it saves 1.44% of the billed-equivalent tokens against the
47	// count's 1.58%, with 17 sessions costlier against 20, and by construction never clears a result of the turn in hand;
48	// what the replay cannot see, the agent reading again what was cleared, is the experiment still to run
49	// (research/output-lifetime-2026-10-22). The proxy itself stays off until then: nothing points an agent at it.
50	// **`turn` sends `keepMin`, a constant, since 2026-11-02.** It used to send the count of the turn's tool uses, which grows
51	// by one with every call of the turn, and the server does not take a growing keep the way the replay modelled it: read
52	// from this machine's proxy log beside Claude Code's own transcripts, each increment un-cleared one earlier result
53	// (the server's `cleared_tool_uses` fell 108, 107, 106 ... as keep rose 3, 4, 5 ...), so the edited prompt differed
54	// from the one just cached at a result near its top, and everything after the system prompt was written again:
55	// 152 calls running in one session, 100k-236k tokens each, read pinned at 31,520. Over 30 days a long session rewrote
56	// its prefix on 1.2% of calls before its first clear and 1.4% held out, on 23.6% after it; 95% of the calls where the
57	// cleared set moved rewrote, 4% where it stayed; and when keep did not change between calls, 5%. At list it was -$801
58	// on the 16 sessions that cleared in the week to 2026-11-01, 4 of them ahead. A constant keep changes the cleared set
59	// only as the conversation grows at its end, where the rewrite is the tail. The name stays for configs that say `turn`;
60	// the Responses proxy keeps the turn by itself (transformResponses) and is not affected.
61	// Bigger cuts, less often (2026-10-28, the owner's call on the replay below). A clear rewrites the prompt cache
62	// from the first result it removes, and a 1h write costs ~200% of an input token against ~2.5% for a read, so what
63	// a clear costs is the rewrite and what it saves is every later read of what it took. Clearing from 100k paid that
64	// rewrite for the smallest cut it could make. Taking the call text and the earlier thinking with it already helped
65	// (they ride the same rewrite); raising the threshold is the other half, and it is where the harm was.
66	// `thinker proxy replay`, 264 Claude Code sessions, 1.05B billed-equivalent tokens, $3,750 at list:
67	//   100k/80k  +inputs +thinking  +7.8% at list  (<60 req -0.7%, 60-119 +1.2%, 120+ +10.9%, 12 sessions costlier)
68	//   140k/100k +inputs +thinking  +7.3% at list  (<60 req -0.1%, 60-119 +0.5%, 120+ +10.2%,  6 sessions costlier)
69	//   180k/140k +inputs +thinking  +5.8% at list  (<60 req +0.1%, 60-119 +0.7%, 120+  +8.0%,  4 sessions costlier)
70	// 140k gives up half a point of the saving to halve the sessions it can cost, and no long session is costlier.
71	// Still not measured, and the reason the holdout stays: the model reading again what was cleared, which the replay
72	// cannot see (proxy-replay.js).
73	export const PROXY_DEFAULTS = { upstream: 'https://api.anthropic.com', trigger: 140000, keep: 'turn', keepMin: 3, keepTurns: 2, clearAtLeast: 100000, holdout: 0, clearInputs: true, clearThinking: false, clearDeep: true, clearNotice: true };
74	// The clearing policy -- clear, freeze what was cleared, and clear again when it pays -- is clearing.js. What this
75	// file does for it is measure the request (`measureClearing`) and send the edit it decides (`transformRequest`,
76	// `cfg.record`). `clearDeep: false` (`--no-clear-deep`, `proxy: { clearDeep: false }`) keeps every ask at the floor.
77	// What a clear takes before the turn, as the API counts what it cleared: the results, and with `clearInputs` the
78	// text of their calls too (an ask that counted the results alone stopped the API half way, since the inputs it cleared
79	// with them counted toward the ask: 296k of inputs beside 345k of results in one session here).
80	// Less the newest `keep` tool uses before the turn, which the server never clears: counted in, they put the ask past
81	// what the server can meet, and an ask it cannot meet is an edit it does not apply at all. On 2026-11-02 (smoke5,
82	// mlflow PR26265) the policy asked 182k at a turn boundary with 120k cleared and 89k in the three kept results, the
83	// server cleared nothing on that call and the whole conversation came back uncleared: 171k read and 73k written for
84	// nothing, then the floor ask again the next call (`proxy-clear-unmet`).
85	export function clearableBeforeTurn(cfg, messages, keep = keepValue(cfg, messages)) {
86	  const textLen = c => typeof c === 'string' ? c.length : Array.isArray(c) ? c.reduce((a, b) => a + (typeof b?.text === 'string' ? b.text.length : 0), 0) : 0;
87	  const results = [], inputs = [];
